2. In `src/context/contentstackContext.tsx`, expand the context to manage live preview state: add `previewData` (hash string), `isPreview` boolean, `editMode` boolean, and a `setPreviewData` setter; parse `window.location.hash` and query params on mount and on `hashchange`/`popstate` events; expose these values via the context provider.

3. In `src/pages/_app.tsx`, wrap the app component tree with the expanded `ContentstackProvider` from `src/context/contentstackContext.tsx` so all pages and hooks can consume preview state; ensure the provider sits above all page content in the render tree.

4. In `src/hooks/useContent.ts`, consume the `ContentstackContext` via `useContext`; add `previewData` and `isPreview` to the dependency array of the content-fetching effect so that when preview state changes, content is re-fetched and the component re-renders.

5. In `src/services/pageService.ts`, update all Contentstack query methods (e.g., `getPage`, `getHomepage`) to accept an optional `previewParams` object and pass it as `live_preview` config to the Stack `Entry.query()` chain, e.g., `.includeReference('...').toJSON().fetch(previewParams)`.

6. In `src/api/utils/_contentstack_getNewsArticles.ts`, update the news articles fetch function to accept an optional `previewParams` argument and forward it to the Contentstack query so previewed (unpublished) article entries are returned during live preview sessions.

7. In `src/interface/content/page.ts`, add type definitions for preview-related structures: `LivePreviewConfig` interface with `hash`, `preview_token`, `edit_mode`, and `previewEnvironment` fields; update `Page` interface if needed to include optional preview metadata.

8. In `src/components/pages/Homepage.tsx`, consume `useContent` (which now reacts to preview state changes) and ensure the component subscribes to context so that when `previewData` updates, the homepage re-renders with the latest previewed content without a full page reload.

